{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces","id":1467680,"title":"Turn body into elemental [Forces]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-13T08:10:35-08:00","id":1467680,"title":"Turn body into elemental [Forces]","content":"The books don't give any detail how turning your body into an element works, other than saying it's Life 3/Forces 3. I have some questions that I know that have no RAW answers, but I still would like to know opinions and ideas.<br /> So, the mage can turn his body into any kind of element. And for each element the same set of questions applies:<br /> <br /> 1- How tangible you are?<br /> 2- How and how fast do you move?<br /> 3- Do you take damage somehow?<br /> <br /> The list of elements i can think is extensive: Fire, Water, Air, Earth, Electricity, Gravity, Magnetism, Shadow, Light.<br /> <br /> If I were to answer the set of questions I would say, for Fire and Air:<br /> <br /> 1- Intangible, can pass through objects and walls<br /> 2- regular speed, flying<br /> 3- By water for Fire. I can't see Air body taking damage<br /> <br /> For Water and Earth:<br /> <br /> 1- Tangible, but can slide thorugh small holes<br /> 2-regular speed, walking or sliding <br /> 3- By fire/heat for Water. By regular impact damage for Earth<br /> <br /> Now, Electricity, Gravity, Magnetism, Shadow and Light are a bit more complicated:<br /> <br /> 1- All Intangible, can pass through objects and walls<br /> 2- Speed of light, flying<br /> 3- That's a tough one. Shadow might take damage from light. I can't see the others taking damage.<br /> <br /> And one last question that probably has the same answer independent of the element: How much successes are needed for this?<br /> <br /> Please, give your opinion and feel free to add any suggestion or observation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T09:47:09-08:00","id":1467687,"title":"","content":"I would house rule that water or earth require Matter 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T13:56:13-08:00","id":1467719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces#post1467680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the mage can turn his body into any kind of element. And for each element the same set of questions applies:<br /> <br /> 1- How tangible you are?<br /> 2- How and how fast do you move?<br /> 3- Do you take damage somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the kind of thing that I think would be immensely impacted by Paradigm, because the underlying questions are:<br /> <br /> 1 - What is an element?<br /> 2 - What is an elemental body?<br /> 3 - What does it mean for a human being to turn into this thing?<br /> <br /> I can think of a number of ways to answer those questions that shouldn't have precedence over the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T23:37:56-08:00","id":1467769,"title":"","content":"Seems like the sort of thing where what you're trying to do is important.<br /> <br /> Life 3/Forces 3 would, IMO be sufficient to turn your body to energy and back. IE, turn your body to electricity to travel along a wire at high speeds, then back again.<br /> <br /> But at that point you're just ordinary electricity, you're as tangible as electricity in a wire, or a lightning bolt.<br /> <br /> You would move with the same speed as electricity. AKA 300 Million Meters a second down a wire. But electricity doesn't just walk down the street. It needs a conduit.<br /> <br /> Obviously you would take damage by anything that disrupts the quantity of energy that you have become. Say you get caught in a circuit and then it shorts out. Or a battery and melted.<br /> <br /> To actually do more than just turn into an energy wave and back, I'd suggest you would need life 5. To create a unique energy based lifeform pattern. With some kind of electrical organs and such. At which point you would basically be vulnerable to anything that could disrupt those organs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T10:29:01-08:00","id":1467800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467769#post1467769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To actually do more than just turn into an energy wave and back, I'd suggest you would need life 5. To create a unique energy based lifeform pattern. With some kind of electrical organs and such. At which point you would basically be vulnerable to anything that could disrupt those organs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you need 5 for this. 4 should be enough.<br /> <br /> Were still talking about a Mage transforming just themselves, and not going on detail about how much control the Mage have over the new form parameters of size and mass. We already have Forces 3 in the middle to take care of details in the new body. That's still clearly below Life 5.<br /> <br /> Life 5 would be to develop the details of this body from scratch and/or apply it to another. The ST may have to make a call about size and mass, but as long as the Mage doesn't make a point about not being of same size and mass or whatever the ST decides, there's no reason for Life 5.<br /> <br /> But yeah, now that I'm actually paying attention to the levels, Life 3/Forces 3 should transform you <i>into an amount of an element</i>, not into an elemental body proper. You're just an inert mass of stuff without agency without other Spheres, with the returning point baked into the magic.<br /> <br /> You're not only targeting yourself, but also using Life 3 to protect your Life Pattern during the transformation, but that's about that. You should need Mind to retain consciousness in any significant level and overall have to use Magic for any action whatsoever beyond staying there or going where your constitutional element naturally goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T14:10:32-08:00","id":1467823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467719#post1467719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the kind of thing that I think would be immensely impacted by Paradigm, because the underlying questions are:<br /> <br /> 1 - What is an element?<br /> 2 - What is an elemental body?<br /> 3 - What does it mean for a human being to turn into this thing?<br /> <br /> I can think of a number of ways to answer those questions that shouldn't have precedence over the other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1- I understand element as the description of the Forces sphere in M20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a metaphysical level, the Forces Sphere commands<br /> energetic Patterns: fire, air, momentum, gravity, radiation,<br /> light, sound, and radio waves\u2026 the kinetic elements that shape<br /> and channel Earthly forces. </div> </div> </div>2- Is turning the &quot;material&quot; of your body into that element.<br /> <br /> 3- Excellent question. It makes no sense for a mage to simply turn into a lump of the element. Turning yourself in a unconscious ammount of fire or electricity makes no sense. So I can only imagine that you simply aren't made of flesh and bones anymore, only the new element. Having to use Mind to retain consciousness makes aboslutely no sense at all.<br /> <br /> Also, you don't have to create a &quot;biological&quot; explanation for this new form. You don't have to explain how your nervous system works, or you digestive system. You are just yourself, but now made of energy. It's magic. If we goes this deep into the science about this effect it will not work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\">Enginseer-42</a>[/B];n1467719]<br /> Seems like the sort of thing where what you're trying to do is important.<br /> <br /> Life 3/Forces 3 would, IMO be sufficient to turn your body to energy and back. IE, turn your body to electricity to travel along a wire at high speeds, then back again.<br /> <br /> But at that point you're just ordinary electricity, you're as tangible as electricity in a wire, or a lightning bolt.<br /> <br /> You would move with the same speed as electricity. AKA 300 Million Meters a second down a wire. But electricity doesn't just walk down the street. It needs a conduit.<br /> <br /> Obviously you would take damage by anything that disrupts the quantity of energy that you have become. Say you get caught in a circuit and then it shorts out. Or a battery and melted.<br /> <br /> To actually do more than just turn into an energy wave and back, I'd suggest you would need life 5. To create a unique energy based lifeform pattern. With some kind of electrical organs and such. At which point you would basically be vulnerable to anything that could disrupt those organs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Life 3/ Forces 3 is the combination present in M20 table for this effect.<br /> <br /> And electricity can move in any medium, including air (that's what lightning does). It is just easier in conduit.<br /> <br /> But as I said, I am not seeing the mage turning himself into a lightning bolt or a piece of Shadow. I am imagining the mage retaining his humanoid body, but now made of a certain element and having some special properties depending on the element. I believe that's what the effect is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T23:05:03-08:00","id":1467859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467823#post1467823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand element as the description of the Forces sphere in M20</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's a casual use of the word instead of a hard definition of element.<br /> <br /> Not that it doesn't define what are the limits on the effects based on Sphere used, but it doesn't answer what element <i>means</i>, just lists them in the context of the Sphere. And this isn't enough to explain a body made of that stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467823#post1467823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is turning the &quot;material&quot; of your body into that element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then by all means you're just a &quot;lump&quot; of stuff. If the effect of the spell is just making your body change composition, then the new composition applies and it is just a pure lump of stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467823#post1467823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes no sense for a mage to simply turn into a lump of the element. Turning yourself in a unconscious ammount of fire or electricity makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You understand how that element work and you can direct it with the same level of Forces or lower. You can simply weave the intended action in the spell.<br /> <br /> The effect isn't then simply &quot;turn into an element and figure what to do later&quot; but more like: turn into electricity, travel through this line in such direction, go back in the desired spot. Turn into fire and stay in the raging inferno until the fires die out to survive it. Fly or swim in a given direction as pure sound, then turn back at reaching the desired spot. Turn into radiation and engulf enemies for 3 turns each.<br /> <br /> Just off the top of my head. I can think of many ways you can make a good use of just becoming a lump of <i>pure energy</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467823#post1467823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having to use Mind to retain consciousness makes aboslutely no sense at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't need the ability to impart thought upon inanimate matter or in any form exist beyond your brain to stay conscious in a state in which you don't actually have a brain?<br /> <br /> Although I have nothing against not using Mind for this, I wouldn't say it doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467823#post1467823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you don't have to create a &quot;biological&quot; explanation for this new form.</div> </div> </div> </div>You definitely have to. That's the whole point of a Paradigm. You don't have to create an explanation that is scientifically accurate, but you need your own explanation on the effect, for every effect.<br /> <br /> That's how Mage: the Ascension have worked since always. It isn't as hard as it seems, but there's just no such a thing as an effect without an explanation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467823#post1467823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 3/ Forces 3 is the combination present in M20 table for this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the combination for an effect that the book states as transforming your body into an element. The actual written text where this effect is cited does not qualify this body in any way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467823#post1467823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as I said, I am not seeing the mage turning himself into a lightning bolt or a piece of Shadow. I am imagining the mage retaining his humanoid body, but now made of a certain element and having some special properties depending on the element. I believe that's what the effect is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes expressly against the description of Life Sphere, hence why I changed my mind when I stopped to consider levels.<br /> <br /> Life 3 only lets you limited changes, insufficient to change into anything that isn't strictly Human. So a body made of a fundamentally distinct substance is well beyond the scope of this level.<br /> <br /> So it isn't a Life effect using Forces to source the body. It is a Forces 3 Effect using Life to let your own body work as &quot;fuel&quot;, then revert back.<br /> <br /> Changing your body so fundamentally as to be a different creature, even if paired with other Spheres to give new properties to this new body, is strictly and explicitly a Life 4 effect, and even then with a lot of limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T12:19:08-08:00","id":1467899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467859#post1467859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effect isn't then simply &quot;turn into an element and figure what to do later&quot; but more like: turn into electricity, travel through this line in such direction, go back in the desired spot. Turn into fire and stay in the raging inferno until the fires die out to survive it. Fly or swim in a given direction as pure sound, then turn back at reaching the desired spot. Turn into radiation and engulf enemies for 3 turns each.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your point now. But the effect isn't turn into unconscious energy, travel and then turn human back, although that is an effect and very useful too. But my idea is to just turn into an element and stay in this form for the duration of the spell or until changing back. <br /> <br /> And I'm going for the M20 table that states that Life 3/Forces 3 is required. Also, the effect is not described as traveling in the form of energy, but only turning yourself into energy. Since it doesn't use Mind, according to your logic you are dead right after casting the spell.<br /> <br /> Life 3 let you turn youself into animals and you retain your conscious in the effect.<br /> <br /> Having said that, considering the effect as just turning into an element and a paradigm similar to Hermetic one (consider that you are now like a D&amp;D elemental), how could that work regarding my op questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:10:15-08:00","id":1467954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467899#post1467899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life 3 let you turn youself into animals and you retain your conscious in the effect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not so. Transforming into an animal is absolutely Life 4 and you explicitly need Mind in order to retain your human mind while in animal form, or else you are limited by the physical mental capacity of the animal and you begin to think like that animal. You will quickly forget you are even human until the magick wears off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 11-15-2021, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T08:04:05-08:00","id":1468005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1467954#post1467954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so. Transforming into an animal is absolutely Life 4 and you explicitly need Mind in order to retain your human mind while in animal form, or else you are limited by the physical mental capacity of the animal and you begin to think like that animal. You will quickly forget you are even human until the magick wears off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you? Shapeshifting is listed as Life 4 or 5 alone in the quick chart. There's no mention of Mind. Indeed, I think it would be the other way around, with Mind being necessary to alter a person's mind into that of an animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T11:28:54-08:00","id":1468026,"title":"","content":"The Mind part is unclear because the book haven't been always consistent on how to deal with this kind of situation. I'd say it is an ST call.<br /> <br /> But the transformation into something markedly non-human is clearly the purview of Life 4, and the transformation into a Water or Earth &quot;Elemental&quot; is completely outside the Sphere of Forces.<br /> <br /> At this point I think that reading the title of a sample rote as equal to D&amp;D's Elemental Body is straight up ignore Mage's RAW, for whatever it's worth.<br /> <br /> If you really want to go that route, I'd say it is simpler to just base it on D&amp;D and legends about elemental creatures, as they are purported to be made of an element, but not actually intangible or anything. Throw in some modification to traits, add a couple special actions based on the element, and the option to &quot;subsume&quot; in the element, in which the Mage is immersed and indistinct from the surrounding element, behaving as normal for it, until they decide to retake cohesion.<br /> <br /> Yet, my personal take is that such a rote would actually be Life 4, Forces 3, Matter 3, Mind 1. Mind in that case to adapt perception to this new state of being and create the set of senses needed for the Elemental Body. With Life 3 I can imagine something similar, but still using Matter 3 and Mind 1, but this time with less cohesion as it isn't an &quot;Elemental Creature&quot;, just the translation of your body into an &quot;Elemental Construct&quot; of sorts.<br /> <br /> Do not take my recommendation on just basing it on D&amp;D as being dismissive as some people around here do sometimes. I was from post 1 thinking that the D&amp;D take on Elementals was already a good starting point for a Hermetic take on the rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T11:47:46-08:00","id":1468030,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> you completely miss the point. I don't want to transform into a D&amp;D elemental. I was just using them as an example of how this effect could look like and maybe it's not even a good example.<br /> <br /> The subject of the thread is the M20 &quot;turn body into element&quot; effect with Life 3/Forces 3 (the thread title is missing Life)<br /> <br /> Now, my argument is that the effect isn't &quot;turn body into element, do X and turn back into human&quot;. This would be a different, more complex, more success needing effect.<br /> So, as soon as you cast this spell you're dead. Game over for you, make another sheet. This makes no sense.<br /> <br /> It's obvious to me that the intention in this effect was to make your mage a human torch, or a body of water, looking like an elemental (not necessarily sharing their traits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:08:14-08:00","id":1468034,"title":"","content":"I always thought it was a Life 4/Forces 4 effect to turn your entire body into fire (Human Torch style) and Life 4/Matter 4 to become solid gold that can move (like a moving Oscars statue).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T13:18:15-08:00","id":1468045,"title":"","content":"No, who isn't understanding my point is you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468030#post1468030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to transform into a D&amp;D elemental. I was just using them as an example of how this effect could look like and maybe it's not even a good example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly understood since your first post.<br /> <br /> What I said is that D&amp;D actually <b>is</b> the best example at hand on how to model such transformation. It is simple, and follow mostly the same rules of a normal character. It also assumes promptly human-like shape and size.<br /> <br /> The major difference is solidity, yet this is actually a feature since you specifically <b>don't</b> want to be a lump of stuff, and permanently insubstantial bodies are actually more limiting than useful, especially when you're not as insubstantial, but made of a form of energy (no phasing through stuff or anything, possibly blocked or harmed by things that don't harm humans).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468030#post1468030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subject of the thread is the M20 &quot;turn body into element&quot; effect with Life 3/Forces 3 (the thread title is missing Life)</div> </div> </div> </div>If the subject of the thread is the specific effect, this effect must follow the rules for the Spheres cited.<br /> <br /> Life 3 specifies that you can't give yourself any property that would result in you being anything other than a human being, regardless of other Spheres, because this is the purview of higher levels in Life. This is RAW, no way around it.<br /> <br /> Forces operates on, and I quote, &quot;<i>the <u><b>kinetic</b></u> elements that shape and channel Earthly forces</i>&quot;. There is no reading of the Sphere that allows for water or earth and other &quot;elements&quot; with substance. Even air is only there as a reference to winds.<br /> <br /> But Forces 3 does specify that it can transmute thing into simple amounts of a given force with help of other Spheres. So you have Life 3 - to target your own body with some sort of transmutation - and Forces 3 - to transmute one thing into and control <i>a lump of stuff</i>.<br /> <br /> None of them has the power to create a complex organism out of whatever, not even out of another complex organism.<br /> <br /> You can, since the subject of the Thread is primarily the effect, ignore the actual rules and roll with another interpretation of the effect based on its name. This is A) valid and B) interesting, but <b>isn't C) RAW</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468030#post1468030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, my argument is that the effect isn't &quot;turn body into element, do X and turn back into human&quot;. This would be a different, more complex, more success needing effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you want a really convoluted action, it most definitely isn't complex or need more than 1 or 2 successes.<br /> <br /> Yet you can go with the idea of consciousness being kept in place, so you have some latitude of deliberate action. I said already it is an interpretation of the rules, but not one you need to follow by RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468030#post1468030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as soon as you cast this spell you're dead. Game over for you, make another sheet. This makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, this makes no sense, yet you're the one repeating it.<br /> <br /> Being baked into the spell, the Life Sphere naturally protects your Life Pattern. There is no reason to believe that once the effect worn out you're dead. I don't know why you keep bringing it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468030#post1468030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's obvious to me that the intention in this effect was to make your mage a human torch, or a body of water, looking like an elemental (not necessarily sharing their traits).</div> </div> </div> </div>Obvious isn't exactly a word that goes well with Mage, but you may be right.<br /> <br /> I won't argue that the idea of the rote may very well be what you are thinking and, yet, it changes nothing.<br /> <br /> Rotes aren't rules. Spheres are. Your interpretation being right just means the rote is wrong. Wouldn't be the first time this happened at any edition of Mage.<br /> <br /> But if the effect you refer to is the one I found in M20 Core, page 508:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Transform a Body into an Element</b><br /> Life 3+/ [appropriate elemental Sphere] 3+<br /> (Life 4+/ 3+[appropriate Sphere]) </div> </div> </div>This is far less straightforward than you say. I see <b>nothing</b> here saying the result is an elemental body and not a lump of stuff. It doesn't say anything to the effect that the result is the Mage becoming a human torch or whatever.<br /> <br /> It just says <i>turn body into an element</i>, and in fact doesn't even say that you should expect this body to remain alive after the effect.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also it doesn't say you should expect your full picture of the effect at the lowest level, it just give a baseline for anything that can be called &quot;turn body into an element&quot;.<br /> <br /> Please give a book and page if it is another effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Added EDIT paragraph. 11-16-2021, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T20:10:59-08:00","id":1468092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468045#post1468045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfectly understood since your first post.<br /> <br /> What I said is that D&amp;D actually <b>is</b> the best example at hand on how to model such transformation. It is simple, and follow mostly the same rules of a normal character. It also assumes promptly human-like shape and size.<br /> <br /> The major difference is solidity, yet this is actually a feature since you specifically <b>don't</b> want to be a lump of stuff, and permanently insubstantial bodies are actually more limiting than useful, especially when you're not as insubstantial, but made of a form of energy (no phasing through stuff or anything, possibly blocked or harmed by things that don't harm humans).</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends. An Earth elemental is completely solid. An Air or Fire elemental is as much tangible as air or fire. This means that you can feel it, but you can't break it. It also might mean that it can pass through small holes, just as air does. And if you consider the weirder ones (Light, Shadow, Gravity, etc..) then you are now completely intangible and can &quot;phase through&quot; several things depending on what you're turning. Sound can easily pass around objects and through holes, etc. It's pratically phasing.<br /> <br /> Another good reason to turn into energy is to travel safely and quickly. This is no limiting at all. Travelling at the speed of light as a lightning or as a laser is very cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468045#post1468045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the subject of the thread is the specific effect, this effect must follow the rules for the Spheres cited.<br /> <br /> Life 3 specifies that you can't give yourself any property that would result in you being anything other than a human being, regardless of other Spheres, because this is the purview of higher levels in Life. This is RAW, no way around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Life 3 says is that &quot;that mage can work <b>substantial</b> alterations on himself. (...) He remains essentially human, but begins to master the definition of `human`&quot;. Now, this is very vague.The mage can, with Life 3, give himself, gills, claws, wings, tentacles, and so forth. In the end he will be so messed up that he will look less human than the &quot;elemental&quot; we are talking about. Mage is very subjective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468045#post1468045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces operates on, and I quote, &quot;<i>the <u><b>kinetic</b></u> elements that shape and channel Earthly forces</i>&quot;. There is no reading of the Sphere that allows for water or earth and other &quot;elements&quot; with substance. Even air is only there as a reference to winds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I grant you, as others users posted too, that Water and Earth might fall under Matter. We can ignore those 2 elements for this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468045#post1468045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Forces 3 does specify that it can transmute thing into simple amounts of a given force with help of other Spheres. So you have Life 3 - to target your own body with some sort of transmutation - and Forces 3 - to transmute one thing into and control <i>a lump of stuff</i>.<br /> <br /> None of them has the power to create a complex organism out of whatever, not even out of another complex organism.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no organism being created. It's you. Why the hell would a mage cast an effect where he lost his counsciousness? You can ask the same question in a Life/Matter effect where you turn into a chair to spy someone. Does the mage lost his consciousness during the effect? Well, probably not! I would go further and say that he should add a sleeping effect in this spell or add Mind to stop his mind from working.<br /> <br /> Also, does the mage <b>wants</b> to remain conscious? Everything depend on how the effect is made and what are its intentions. Would the mage be able to walk as a chair? Well, did he implemented that into the spell? If so, then yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468045#post1468045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can, since the subject of the Thread is primarily the effect, ignore the actual rules and roll with another interpretation of the effect based on its name. This is A) valid and B) interesting, but <b>isn't C) RAW</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. On the other hand we can't talk RAW about this effect because it's a simple f***ing line in a table. There is no description and all we can do is give our interpretations based on descriptions of other completely different effects. The only thing we have to agree that is RAW is that you can turn into an element. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468045#post1468045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet you can go with the idea of consciousness being kept in place, so you have some latitude of deliberate action. I said already it is an interpretation of the rules, but not one you need to follow by RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's what I was asking in OP. Considering you made the spell in a way you keep your consciousness, how would you answer the 3 questions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468045#post1468045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rotes aren't rules. Spheres are. Your interpretation being right just means the rote is wrong. Wouldn't be the first time this happened at any edition of Mage.<br /> <br /> But if the effect you refer to is the one I found in M20 Core, page 508:<br /> <br /> This is far less straightforward than you say. I see <b>nothing</b> here saying the result is an elemental body and not a lump of stuff. It doesn't say anything to the effect that the result is the Mage becoming a human torch or whatever.<br /> <br /> It just says <i>turn body into an element</i>, and in fact doesn't even say that you should expect this body to remain alive after the effect.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also it doesn't say you should expect your full picture of the effect at the lowest level, it just give a baseline for anything that can be called &quot;turn body into an element&quot;.<br /> <br /> Please give a book and page if it is another effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is this entry. I can't remember if it's stated somewhere else. It is not a rote it's an effect on the magical chart. Those <b>are rules</b>. And I agree that it's as vague as it could be, and that's why I came here asking for opinions. It also doesn't say you are now inanimate either.And if an effect doesn't explicity says that the mage lost his conscious mind, I prefer to believe that he doesn't<br /> <br /> If you are going to tell me that the best you can think about this description is turning yourself into a useless piece of element, then you indeed can't help me here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T05:40:43-08:00","id":1468119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces#post1467680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books don't give any detail how turning your body into an element works, other than saying it's Life 3/Forces 3. I have some questions that I know that have no RAW answers, but I still would like to know opinions and ideas.<br /> So, the mage can turn his body into any kind of element. And for each element the same set of questions applies:<br /> <br /> 1- How tangible you are?<br /> 2- How and how fast do you move?<br /> 3- Do you take damage somehow?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll actually answer the questions as asked, but first I'll say again that if it were my game the effect as you describe would require Life 4 <i>(Edit: I can probably be convinced it should be Life 3)</i> and Mind (at least 1). I would also rule that all such transformations, regardless of if they are Forces or Matter, require Forces 3 if you want to be able to move in a human-like manner in your new form. Otherwise you will move in the manner of the Force/Matter (i.e. Earth will just be an inanimate statue, Fire and Air will rapidly dissipate, and Water will instantly form a puddle and start to seep into the ground.<br /> <br /> I will also say that Earth, Air, and Water (and even Fire, probably) are NOT Forces, they are Matter. Even though they are the classic &quot;Elements&quot; of Western occultism/magic/Airbender lore, they are still matter. Earth is soil, dirt, stone - definitely not Forces. Water is the chemical H2O, definitely not Forces. Air is a mixture of mostly Nitrogen and Oxygen, definitely not Forces. Even Fire is not energy itself, but the material expression of matter combusting under extremely high heat. Though &quot;heat&quot; falls under Forces, you specifically state that you want to turn into &quot;Fire&quot;, not heat. Fire is Matter, unless you are actually talking about heat, which is Forces.<br /> <br /> So to turn into animate Earth/Air/Fire/Water would be a Life 4(3)/Forces 3+/ Matter 3 Effect. To turn into a Force (Light, Heat, Gravity, Electricity, Magnetism, etc.) would be Life 4(3)/Forces 3+.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shadow&quot; is not a thing, it is the absence of a thing, and so does not fall under any of the pattern spheres. So, you cannot turn into Shadow unless maybe with high Entropy sphere magick, ala Obtenebration/Abyss lore. However, you can <i>appear</i> as a shadow - if you convert yourself to Light and control the forces around you to absorb light, you will appear as inky nothingness floating or walking around, which could very well be described as &quot;Shadow&quot;.<br /> <br /> To answer the questions then!<br /> <br /> <b>Quesiton 1:</b><br /> If you turn yourself into animate Matter (Earth/Air/Fire/Water), then it depends. Earth is quite tangible but can &quot;flow&quot; under the right conditions. Air, Fire, and Water are tangible, but also easily conform to shapes and can pass thorough small openings. Forces are in general less tangible than Matter. Light seems intangible, but cannot pass through opaque matter. Heat can pass through matter, but the speed it can do so depends on the matter. Electricity can pass through conductive Matter very rapidly and almost not at all through non-conductive matter. Magnetism and Gravity are not hindered by matter for the most part, but if you're out in the depths of space stay away from large gravity wells and high energy events, like stars, neutron stars, pulsars, magnetars, and black holes.<br /> <br /> <b>Quesiton 2:</b><br /> For animate matter (Earth/Air/Fire/Water), not very fast. Probably just stick to normal human speed walking on ground, though since you are using Forces 3 to move, you can just as easily fly by manipulating how gravity interacts with you. I once calculated that with Forces 2 (manipulating the vector of Earth gravity, but not its magnitude), you can fly at approximately 125 mph (200 kph). Basically you max out at the terminal velocity of a human falling through Earth's atmosphere, since you can't enhance the magnitude of the gravity. With Forces 3 both manipulating the vector and magnitude of Earth gravity, you can fly much faster, at least 500 and probably 1000 mph (1600 kph). You need to protect yourself from the friction against the atmosphere at this point, so wear a helmet and try not to collide with a bird.<br /> <br /> For animate forces (Light/Heat/Gravity/Electricity/Magnetism), it's faster. So fast, in essence, that you don't need to worry about the speeds unless you are trying to get to another planet. However I personally would rule that you are not a &quot;natural force&quot; and you are in fact using Forces 3+ to control your &quot;movement&quot;, and so are limited by how much Force you can apply. I'd use the 1000 mph (1600 kph) listed above for the Forces 3 movement speed. Higher Forces would produce faster speeds.<br /> <br /> <b>Quesiton 3:</b><br /> Yes, but not generally from physical things. Even when turning into &quot;Earth&quot; you couldn't exactly be hurt by a hammer. If you were made of stone and got physically broken into smaller stones, then you would still be made of stone and so... no actual &quot;damage&quot;. But weird things might damage you instead depending on the ST. For example, if you were Water and encountered sufficient heat, you might turn to steam or vapor and some ST's might call that &quot;damage&quot;. I would say, however, that it's still water and so not &quot;damage&quot;. Short of all the Matter/Forces of your new &quot;body&quot; being completely vaporized to nothing, you really can't be hurt or killed. Direct Effects though would still work - Entropy 4 or a Prime 3 energy blast still does aggravated damage to your pattern, and the use of Forces 3+ (against Light/Heat/Gravity/Electricity/Magnetism) or Matter 3+ (against Earth/Air/Fire/Water) can still tear apart your new Forces or Matter pattern, after all. You'd be immune to Life 3+ damage, however, at least without the aggressor combining it with Forces/Matter 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 11-17-2021, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T06:15:34-08:00","id":1468123,"title":"","content":"My two cents:<br /> <br /> On the subject of what Spears should be required, I also would insist on Life as well as Forces, in that you are transforming a Life Pattern into a Forces Pattern; so you need the sphere that covers what you're transforming from as well as the sphere that covers what you're transforming to. I would not require Mind; but if you don't include it, your mind will gradually deteriorate the longer you stay in the elemental form; much like if you transform into an animal and don't take special effort to preserve your mind, you will gradually lose your higher reasoning facility and become an animal in mind as well as in body. <br /> <br /> Solids and liquids would be covered by Matter rather than Forces; but gas and plasmas (including fire and electricity) would be covered by Forces, as would the likes of light and darkness. (In the scientific paradigm, darkness is the absence of light; but in many other paradigms, darkness is a thing unto itself.) More exotic options, like turning yourself into sound, gamma radiation, or gravity, might be possible, but should be considered carefully. <br /> <br /> As to the effects: for light, materials are either transparent, translucent, or opaque. If they're transparent, you can pretty much ignore them: you'll pass right through them, whether you want to or not. If they're opaque, they'll block you; but on the other hand, you're able to exert your strength against them as if you were still flesh and blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T07:46:56-08:00","id":1468131,"title":"","content":"Altrough not <i>exactly </i>what's being asked, The Rote of OoH Revised Trad Book, &quot;Vulcan's Hammer&quot; could be of interest<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Vulcan's Hammer (Forces 3, Life 4, Matter 3)</b><br /> There are times when subtlety is called for. Vulcan's Hammer is not a rote for those times.<b> This enchantment transforms a mage into a living weapon of iron and flame. </b>The effect is most often focused on a statuette of the mage in question, sculpted from iron-rich clay and hardened under intense heat. Over the course of working the clay, the mage scribes and then kneads her True Name into it 10 separate times, thus concealing the truth of her identity within it and making the statuette a conduit through which her own living pattern may be affected.(Understandably, a magician of the Order does well to carefully protect the focus for this effect, as it contains information about her most intimate being, through which all manner of deleterious magics could work against her.)<br /> <br /> <b>While in the (grossly vulgar) shape of Vulcan's Hammer, the average mage weighs in at just about a ton, and is wreathed in flames of up to 1000 degrees in temperature. Needless to say, there is not much that can stand before the assault, or even the close passing, of such a juggernaut (therefore, beware before using this rote on wooden floors, near gas stations or in a mine shaft, among many other places....)<br /> <br /> System: Vulcan's Hammer grants the following changes to Attributes: +3 Strength, -2 Dexterity (to a minimum of 1,) +4 Stamina. The mage automatically fails all Social Attribute rolls, except those involving intimidation, against any Sleeper who is not aware and accepting of the mage's Awakened nature. She inflicts normal Forces damage on those who come in physical contact with her while in this state.</b> By adding Prime 2 to the rote, the mage can deal aggravated damage with hand-to-hand attacks, soak aggravated damage normally and inflict aggravated damage on any who come in physical contact with her<b>. While in this shape, she is immune to phenomena that specifically target organic beings, is subject to phenomena that affect normal iron (save for Prime 4 Flames of Purification , as she is still a living thing)</b> and is a walking Paradox magnet. Naturally, this effect is always vulgar. </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> Personaly I would agree in the general interpretation of full body modifications, that transform you on another being are <i>Life 4 </i>effects.<br /> <br /> All the examples of Life 3 are for smaller changes. Yes, if you pile them all together it becomes a total, but that'slike piling up small effects to get a larget one (I can burn a house with a single Forces 4 effect, or use Forces 3 to burn one room at a time, or create a small fire that will spread naturally). Small things like this are where the system starts to break. The ST should decide what's the limit, or if it's correct to allow someone to - say - turn into coughar (normaly Life 4) with Life 3 if they do it one part at a time (fur, claws, fangs, etc...) knowing that this will likely take a lot more successes, if not Paradox. <br /> <br /> Mind doesn't seem to be required to be conscious in an inorganic form, but perhaps this <i>could </i>be one of these things that DO depend on Paradigm/Focus.<br /> <br /> How important it's the nervous system for your mage?. Progenitors have rotes to affect the mind with Life alone trough the brain chemistry beyond, so maybe they DO need Mind 1 or so to &quot;transcribe&quot; the consciousness to a brainless form. On the other hand, many belief systems adscribe &quot;consciousness&quot; lifeless objects and energies. In those cases, it could be interesting to think *how* conscious they are. <br /> <br /> Typically, Life effects that transform your body also affect your <i>senses </i>(get an eagle's body, you get an eagle's far seeing eyes. Get a hound's nose, you get to smell like a hound). What kind of senses do a body of energy/inorganing matter has?. In Ars Magica the OoH had fire being very conscious of the things it burns , but not so much of it's surroundings. \u200bMaybe for some Focuses seeing it's as easy as including <i>eyes</i> into the form (regardless of &quot;neural system&quot;).<br /> <br /> I think this could be interesting, but the simple answer of: &quot;base human&quot; won't be too bad. It seems to be the answer of the rote above (albeit that one has also a humanoid body, so it makes sense in-paradigm)<br /> <br /> Movement / interaction: That of the energy + any other that was determined trough Forces application. Paradigm could determine some &quot;polemical&quot; interactions, like if a ligth body can be damaged by &quot;darkness&quot; and vice-versa. I wouldn't typically invoke natural dispersion, much like how vampiric mist-body can't be easily dispersed trough wind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T07:55:28-08:00","id":1468132,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26904_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26904\" data-vbnamecard=\"26904\">breggie</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> thank so much for your 2 cents.<br /> <br /> I ask that we ignore Earth, Water and Air, since they might fall under Matter. <br /> Also, I forgot the Life on the tittle. I am refering to the Life 3/ Forces 3 effect in M20 chart.<br /> <br /> I think it is more interesting to talk about energies like Light, gravity or electromagnetism. All of those travel at the speed of light. nd gravity seems to ignore completely any obstacle.<br /> <br /> Breggie, I wouldn't say this is a Forces 3 to control movement effect. Also, why are you limiting the speed 1600 km/h? Tou made any calculation? I believe this logic wouldn't apply for something without any mass like electromagnetism.<br /> <br /> For both traveling and defense, I believe turning into electromagnetism (light) or gravity are really good options, because you get lightspeed fast and intangible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T08:03:13-08:00","id":1468133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468132#post1468132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am refering to the Life 3/ Forces 3 effect in M20 chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpret that effect as being a partial body modification. Like Life 3 giving you claws, tentacles or wings - the elemental version. Like, if you want to have hair of ligth it's Life 3/Forces 3: It would look cool, but won't afect travel very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T08:22:08-08:00","id":1468135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468132#post1468132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26904_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26904\" data-vbnamecard=\"26904\">breggie</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> thank so much for your 2 cents.<br /> <br /> I ask that we ignore Earth, Water and Air, since they might fall under Matter. <br /> Also, I forgot the Life on the tittle. I am refering to the Life 3/ Forces 3 effect in M20 chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I was mentioning these in terms of where I'd draw the line. In particular, I'd be inclined to put air under Forces. Note that there are several paradigms that includes the notion of elements, but do not classify air as such \u2014 even when they classify fire as an element. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468132#post1468132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is more interesting to talk about energies like Light, gravity or electromagnetism. All of those travel at the speed of light. nd gravity seems to ignore completely any obstacle.<br /> <br /> Breggie, I wouldn't say this is a Forces 3 to control movement effect. Also, why are you limiting the speed 1600 km/h? Tou made any calculation? I believe this logic wouldn't apply for something without any mass like electromagnetism.<br /> <br /> For both traveling and defense, I believe turning into electromagnetism (light) or gravity are really good options, because you get lightspeed fast and intangible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't grant light-speed travel without Correspondence: even in the scientific paradigm, the properties of individual particles don't necessarily translate to a conglomerate of them: they may be moving in more or less opposite directions, largely cancelling out their individual motions. Outside the scientific paradigm, the notion of \u201cthe speed of light\u201d likely doesn't even <i>exist</i>; but the principle still holds: an elemental composed of light won't automatically behave like beams of light would.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I would have no problem using your body of light as an instrument in a teleportation effect. I would even be willing to make the teleportation effect coincidental on the ground that it doesn't take light any significant time to cover the distance. However, the body of light would be restricted to going where light can go. Through air? Sure! Through smoke? Nope. Your teleportation would end at the edge of the smoke, and you would then have to walk through it normally. Which you could do, because your body of light can interact with the smoke and push it aside the same way that a physical body could.<br /> <br /> I might even allow that body of light based teleportation to be done using Forces. But it would be a separate effect from transforming into and maintaining a body of light. It would not be something that you can automatically do with no effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-17-2021, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T08:26:06-08:00","id":1468136,"title":"","content":"I'll state my last objection before giving my definitive answer to the questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the matter of solidity, what I meant was that D&amp;D adds some solidity to elementals made out of fluids, and I personally think that makes for a more useful transformation, but require Life 4 and Matter 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another good reason to turn into energy is to travel safely and quickly. This is no limiting at all. Travelling at the speed of light as a lightning or as a laser is very cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll talk about limits later, but my suggested version of the effect is perfectly appropriate for travel, so I don't see your point.<br /> <br /> More pressing, though, without enough Mind built in it you're still limited to human perception and reaction. You may be physically capable of traveling at light speed, but definitely not of seeing where you're going when doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this is very vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is indeed. Yet Life 4 clarifies a little more, since it establishes what you can only do from there on, and it includes effective changes to your species.<br /> <br /> Now, I definitely see no sense in the slightest in defining that a human body with artificially added features is less human than a body that is effectively made of an entirely new composition, just because of looks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no organism being created.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a form of speech. Forces 3 don't create Forces-based organisms. Life 4 don't transmute you into another species. None of the two, at those levels, can turn you into an energy-based life form with an entirely new physiology and just the semblance of a human being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the hell would a mage cast an effect where he lost his counsciousness?</div> </div> </div> </div>You ask this, then immediately after you tell me the Mage could, indeed, want this. Just to reach the convoluted conclusion that a Mage should add Mind to suppress their Mind if this is what they want.<br /> <br /> I can't agree with your reasoning here, but I also don't care if the Mage retains their consciousness at least for a time, so I still don't know why you keep arguing over this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand we can't talk RAW about this effect because it's a simple f***ing line in a table.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can. The Spheres have complete descriptions. The list of effects is a list of suggestions and examples to help you grasp how you combine them. The rules are in the Spheres. As it was in every previous edition of Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is this entry.</div> </div> </div> </div>This entry is part of a chart whose function is to provide fast examples of requirements for effects. Those are not rules, hence the fact it is a chart with no details, just a name and requisites.<br /> <br /> It isn't vague. You are outright reading into it several things it didn't said and ignored that the chart also presents a &quot;+&quot; sign next to each number. It isn't a cute mark, it's an indication that the effect can be constructed with varying levels for different purposes.<br /> <br /> You are reading elemental body where such a thing wasn't said, and you are assuming best effect with minimum levels, then adding stuff because you don't think it useful enough with the bare minimum. But that &quot;+&quot; sign pretty much says there is a bare minimum and that is the requirement for a bare minimum effect.<br /> <br /> Bare minimum effect: living body becomes element. Not elementAL, just element. Period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if an effect doesn't explicity says that the mage lost his conscious mind, I prefer to believe that he doesn't</div> </div> </div> </div>What you prefer is perfectly valid, but is different from what you asked. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are going to tell me that the best you can think about this description is turning yourself into a useless piece of element, then you indeed can't help me here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said &quot;lump&quot; in the sense of useless. I meant that you aren't a complex organism made of an exotic substance, just a mass of that element meant to behave as that element behaves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468092#post1468092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's what I was asking in OP. Considering you made the spell in a way you keep your consciousness, how would you answer the 3 questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming a body made entirely of a single Force:<br /> <br /> 1 - You're as tangible as any manifestation of that force, but also affected by the same vicissitudes. You can traverse any medium they can, you can't traverse any medium they can't. More importantly, you're &quot;weakened&quot; in the same way, bent in the same way, and affect the medium in the same way. Any of this may be a bug or a feature depending on the situation. You can't affect things in a manner that force can't.<br /> <br /> 2 - You traverse the same mediums. If you &quot;let go&quot; and just follow the rules of that force, letting yourself be carried to its natural path, you'll have the natural speed of that force. If you move against this natural path, as electricity ignoring cables or light making a curve, then you're limited to your rating and success in the effect as if you were trying to direct that energy with a pure Forces effect.<br /> <br /> 3 - Anytime you loose a sensible amount of energy you should take damage. So, if as light you traverse a material that lets just some light through, like paper, you take damage. As fire you don't want to be doused, as darkness you don't want to be directly illuminated.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Examples:</b></u><br /> <br /> <i><b>Fire</b></i> - You can travel through living fire or through combustible materials, at a natural speed equal to the speed of its spread, but you consume fuel and burn things as you do so. You depend on the Fire Triangle, being barred from natural travel to any place that lack any of the three pillars (fuel, heat and oxygen), and taking damage when one is missing for any reason.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Sound</b></i> - You travel through matter at varying speeds according to the medium, and blocked only by vacuum. But you loose energy when traveling any distance, quickly, and even more if you travel through any place that muffles sound, taking damage every time your potency in decibels is halved. Your movement have all the effects on the area of a sound of equal potency, and probably leaves sound behind you as you &quot;propagates&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Electricity</b></i> - Similar to sound, but with an added effect: things that take energy out of you keep it instead of dissipating it, which usually means structural damage. You can travel through air, but leaves an actual lightning in your path with all that entails.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Gravity</b></i> - You travel at lightspeed deforming space where you stand. While you can travel through anything, in any direction, your only interaction with everything else is to pull things towards you. You also have extreme reach, but not so extreme strength. Remember that the gravity of the entire planet isn't strong enough to stop someone from jumping. It only wins out in the end because it keeps pulling after the jumper stops pressing feet against ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T09:12:47-08:00","id":1468140,"title":"","content":"And here's a more bizarre one: light is massless, but not weightless; according to Relativity, light falls just as quickly as a pebble or a boulder falls; is just that, normally, light doesn't stick around long enough for this to matter. But with a body of light, it does. So a body of light would not even automatically allow you to fly; that, too, would be a separate Forces Effect \u2014 albeit one that, like the teleportation Effect I mentioned above, would probably be Coincidental if using the body of light as an instrument to justify it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T09:26:30-08:00","id":1468141,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Turn a body. Not a body part. A body is an entire body.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> oh ok. Also, I'd say that even shamanic paradigms do believe in lots of science things.<br /> <br /> Monteparnas, you made a good point about the + in the chart. However, it is not Life 4+/ Forces 3+ . it's Life 3+/ Forces 3+. This means two things: there is no mind involved and it starts with both at 3.<br /> <br /> When you turn your mage into a chair for spying a meeting, do you ask for Mind kust to keep your conscience? I can see using Mind to give consciousness or to remove consciousness from a contient being. But not to give conscience to a contient being just because it is changing form. Indeed, when you change you body into an animal YOUR MIND begins to adapt to that form after a while and you start to think as a real cat, which you transformed into. So, you could argue that you could get the mind of a fire (lose your consciousness) if you stay in this form for a long time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468136#post1468136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming a body made entirely of a single Force:<br /> <br /> 1 - You're as tangible as any manifestation of that force, but also affected by the same vicissitudes. You can traverse any medium they can, you can't traverse any medium they can't. More importantly, you're &amp;quot;weakened&amp;quot; in the same way, bent in the same way, and affect the medium in the same way. Any of this may be a bug or a feature depending on the situation. You can't affect things in a manner that force can't.<br /> <br /> 2 - You traverse the same mediums. If you &amp;quot;let go&amp;quot; and just follow the rules of that force, letting yourself be carried to its natural path, you'll have the natural speed of that force. If you move against this natural path, as electricity ignoring cables or light making a curve, then you're limited to your rating and success in the effect as if you were trying to direct that energy with a pure Forces effect.<br /> <br /> 3 - Anytime you loose a sensible amount of energy you should take damage. So, if as light you traverse a material that lets just some light through, like paper, you take damage. As fire you don't want to be doused, as darkness you don't want to be directly illuminated.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Examples:</b></u><br /> <br /> <i><b>Fire</b></i> - You can travel through living fire or through combustible materials, at a natural speed equal to the speed of its spread, but you consume fuel and burn things as you do so. You depend on the Fire Triangle, being barred from natural travel to any place that lack any of the three pillars (fuel, heat and oxygen), and taking damage when one is missing for any reason.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Sound</b></i> - You travel through matter at varying speeds according to the medium, and blocked only by vacuum. But you loose energy when traveling any distance, quickly, and even more if you travel through any place that muffles sound, taking damage every time your potency in decibels is halved. Your movement have all the effects on the area of a sound of equal potency, and probably leaves sound behind you as you &amp;quot;propagates&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Electricity</b></i> - Similar to sound, but with an added effect: things that take energy out of you keep it instead of dissipating it, which usually means structural damage. You can travel through air, but leaves an actual lightning in your path with all that entails.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Gravity</b></i> - You travel at lightspeed deforming space where you stand. While you can travel through anything, in any direction, your only interaction with everything else is to pull things towards you. You also have extreme reach, but not so extreme strength. Remember that the gravity of the entire planet isn't strong enough to stop someone from jumping. It only wins out in the end because it keeps pulling after the jumper stops pressing feet against ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was an excellent answer. That's what I was looking to. You could add electromagnetism/light. I believe it can travel a LOT before getting weak (we see light of stars from the edge of universe) and can travel through any mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T09:28:03-08:00","id":1468142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468136#post1468136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>Examples:</b></u><br /> <br /> <i><b>Fire</b></i> - You can travel through living fire or through combustible materials, at a natural speed equal to the speed of its spread, but you consume fuel and burn things as you do so. You depend on the Fire Triangle, being barred from natural travel to any place that lack any of the three pillars (fuel, heat and oxygen), and taking damage when one is missing for any reason.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Sound</b></i> - You travel through matter at varying speeds according to the medium, and blocked only by vacuum. But you loose energy when traveling any distance, quickly, and even more if you travel through any place that muffles sound, taking damage every time your potency in decibels is halved. Your movement have all the effects on the area of a sound of equal potency, and probably leaves sound behind you as you &quot;propagates&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Electricity</b></i> - Similar to sound, but with an added effect: things that take energy out of you keep it instead of dissipating it, which usually means structural damage. You can travel through air, but leaves an actual lightning in your path with all that entails.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Gravity</b></i> - You travel at lightspeed deforming space where you stand. While you can travel through anything, in any direction, your only interaction with everything else is to pull things towards you. You also have extreme reach, but not so extreme strength. Remember that the gravity of the entire planet isn't strong enough to stop someone from jumping. It only wins out in the end because it keeps pulling after the jumper stops pressing feet against ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are fantastic examples and far better than anything I've thought of on this topic. The entire effect being discussed is not useless, per se, but it's exceptionally dangerous and of situational use at best.<br /> <br /> I'll do my best to add one...<br /> <br /> <i><b>Light</b></i> - You can keep yourself contained in-place and move about slowly, but if you let go in any direction you travel at the speed of light until you collide with an object that blocks you. This will probably result in your death, so be ultra careful. You will likely need Time 1 (and probably Mind 1) to &quot;let go&quot; for precisely the exact amount of time necessary to get where you want to, because at normal human thinking speeds you will end up about 37,500 km beyond your destination (average reaction time is 0.125 seconds, light travels at about 300,000 km/s. 300,000 * 0.125 = 37,500). Without Correspondence/Data 2, you won't be able to see your path to ensure you will survive the trip, but in any case this mode of travel is safest in deep space.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468140#post1468140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here's a more bizarre one: light is massless, but not weightless; according to Relativity, light falls just as quickly as a pebble or a boulder falls; is just that, normally, light doesn't stick around long enough for this to matter. But with a body of light, it does. So a body of light would not even automatically allow you to fly; that, too, would be a separate Forces Effect \u2014 albeit one that, like the teleportation Effect I mentioned above, would probably be Coincidental if using the body of light as an instrument to justify it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if &quot;Light&quot; has mass because it depends on how your specific mage defines &quot;Light&quot;, but a photon does have an exceptionally tiny mass if we're talking about a scientific paradigm. (Edit: unless my physics knowledge is old, or wrong. I am pretty sure photons have mass, but I should have searched that before posting... ssssoooorrrryyyyyyyy.... ^_^ )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 11-17-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T09:33:37-08:00","id":1468144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468141#post1468141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you turn your mage into a chair for spying a meeting, do you ask for Mind kust to keep your conscience? I can see using Mind to give consciousness or to remove consciousness from a contient being. But not to give conscience to a contient being just because it is changing form...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe.<br /> <br /> If you turn yourself into a chair made of matter, then yes absolutely you need to include Mind or else you will simply be a chair and will not be conscious of your surroundings until the effect wears off and you aren't a chair anymore. Even with Mind, you need to use some Level 1 spheres to perceive anything around you because you don't have eyes, ears, or even nerves.<br /> <br /> If instead you turn yourself into a living thing that is just in the shape of a chair with Life 4 (you still have blood, bones, and a brain), then arguably no, you do not need to include Mind. But without Mind, you will likely suffer PTSD afterwards because this sort of transformation would likely be very <b>TRAUMATIC</b>...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 11-17-2021, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T09:42:29-08:00","id":1468145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if &quot;Light&quot; has mass because it depends on how your specific mage defines &quot;Light&quot;, but a photon does have an exceptionally tiny mass if we're talking about a scientific paradigm. </div> </div> </div>I'm risking a thread derailment here; but no, it doesn't. A photon's intrinsic mass is zero; it has momentum and kinetic energy, but not mass \u2014 not in any sense that matters scientifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T13:58:02-08:00","id":1468174,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> photons (light) do not have mass. Nor weight. It is affected by gravity because according to rrlativity gravity is the bemd of spacetime and light travels in spacetime. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26904_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26904\" data-vbnamecard=\"26904\">breggie</a> i liked your description of light, but I don't yhink you would die if hitting an obstacle, but reflect (if its opaque). Light doesn't crase to exist when hitting objects, it just reflects and that's how we can see things.<br /> <br /> I believe electromagnetism would be very similar to light, except that it can travel through some obstacles and can be invisible.<br /> <br /> EDIT: ELECTROMAGNETISM: It will depend of what frequency of the specter you turn into. Light should be reflected by opaque objects and radio can be reflected by electrically conductive materials.However, if you have a high frequency, like gamma rays, you can pass through almost anything. It is necessary several inches of lead or feets of concrete to begin to stop them. They pass conpletely through human body.<br /> Regardless, you always travel at lightspeed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-17-2021, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T14:09:18-08:00","id":1468175,"title":"","content":"Light <i> is </i>electromagnetism.<br /> <br /> At the point is that light falls, and at the same speed that everything else does. So a body of light that isn't moving, or is moving very slowly, will fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T16:03:55-08:00","id":1468188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468175#post1468175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light <i> is </i>electromagnetism.<br /> <br /> At the point is that light falls, and at the same speed that everything else does. So a body of light that isn't moving, or is moving very slowly, will fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. That's why I puted light insise electromagnetism description. Light is part of the EM spectrum. <br /> According to relatovity, norhing &quot;falls&quot;. They just follow their geodesics of the curved spacetime. As does light. I don't know what your point is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T16:15:36-08:00","id":1468189,"title":"","content":"My point is that a body of light would follow its geodesics, i.e. move in freefall, i.e. fall. Thus, from a scientific standpoint, a body of light would not have a built in ability to levitate or fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T16:48:39-08:00","id":1468193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468189#post1468189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that a body of light would follow its geodesics, i.e. move in freefall, i.e. fall. Thus, from a scientific standpoint, a body of light would not have a built in ability to levitate or fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I understand your point. Light's path is affected by gravity making it bend. But unless you're in a black hole gravity is not enough to trap light. For the game purposes, you can ignore the effect of gravity on light and fly. To be fair, you're not flying, you're propagating into one direction. This direction could be &quot;up&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T16:59:53-08:00","id":1468196,"title":"","content":"Not arbitrarily. Breaking his few laws of nature as possible, light would have to obey the law of action and reaction. Thus, the body of light could not spontaneously move up. It would have to push off against the ground. That is, it would have to walk. And it could, so long as you're not trying to walk across glass panes, such as a skylight, or something with no structural integrity, such as a cloud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T17:09:06-08:00","id":1468199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468196#post1468196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not arbitrarily. Breaking his few laws of nature as possible, light would have to obey the law of action and reaction. Thus, the body of light could not spontaneously move up. It would have to push off against the ground. That is, it would have to walk. And it could, so long as you're not trying to walk across glass panes, such as a skylight, or something with no structural integrity, such as a cloud.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Light doesn't travel this way. It moves by the propagation of the generation of the electric and magnetic fields, one generating the other each time. Light doesn't need (nor can, because it's massless) to push the ground to move. You just...propagates... Is that simple. Just like the sound also propagates and you would be able to &quot;fly&quot; as sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T17:13:15-08:00","id":1468201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468199#post1468199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Light doesn't travel this way. It moves by the propagation of the generation of the electric and magnetic fields, one generating the other each time. Light doesn't need (nor can, because it's massless) to push the ground to move. You just...propagates... Is that simple. Just like the sound also propagates and you would be able to &quot;fly&quot; as sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so with a body of light, or else there would be no way for it to stand still. It would be moving strictly at the speed of light, never a millimeter slower or faster. Plus, time dilation would mean that the Mind associated with the body of light would experience no time, and thus would never have time to think of anything throughout the entire duration of the body of light. If you are using the scientific paradigm, that is.<br /> <br /> And that's not a body of light. That's teleportation with the theory of electromagnetics as its rationale.<br /> <br /> Also, photons propagate in essentially the same way that protons and electrons do; it's just that they propagate in the electromagnetic field instead of the proton and electron fields.<br /> <br /> To elaborate further the one rule breaking that I am positing is that the photons in the body of light are linked together into atom-like structures. Whatever it is that's linking them is the magic involved. But the result is that the photons don't propagate in \u201cstraight lines\u201d anymore; they orbit each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-17-2021, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T17:45:59-08:00","id":1468205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468201#post1468201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so with a body of light, or else there would be no way for it to stand still. It would be moving strictly at the speed of light, never a millimeter slower or faster. Plus, time dilation would mean that the Mind associated with the body of light would experience no time, and thus would never have time to think of anything throughout the entire duration of the body of light. If you are using the scientific paradigm, that is.<br /> <br /> And that's not a body of light. That's teleportation with the theory of electromagnetics as its rationale.<br /> <br /> Also, photons propagate in essentially the same way that protons and electrons do; it's just that they propagate in the electromagnetic field instead of the proton and electron fields.<br /> <br /> To elaborate further the one rule breaking that I am positing is that the photons in the body of light are linked together into atom-like structures. Whatever it is that's linking them is the magic involved. But the result is that the photons don't propagate in \u201cstraight lines\u201d anymore; they orbit each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right about everything. I'm not sure about the electron and proton fields, though. I think this is one theory that is not as solid as our knowledge about EM waves. <br /> <br /> Ok, I can see your description being adopted by a ST. And mine too. Just out of curiosity, then would air and fire element also not fly?<br /> <br /> Not that this mstters, because you are using Forces 3 too, so you can add flight easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T18:34:09-08:00","id":1468208,"title":"","content":"For air and fire elementals, they have enough physical form to displace air. So whether or not they float depends on whether they are lighter than air or heavier.<br /> <br /> All of this hammers down heavily on fidelity to science. If that's not so important, Ben things can definitely be different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T19:27:24-08:00","id":1468212,"title":"","content":"The part about falling is a little complicated. Of all the Forces described 'till now, off the top of my head only Gravity would ignore gravity by itself, but for things like electricity, sound and heat, their mediums of propagation are enough to make this a moot point.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, gravity is a &quot;weak force&quot;. Although you can't just ignore it, if Photon-Man makes a jump starting upwards at lightspeed, Earth's gravity will have negligible effect in the trajectory.<br /> <br /> Either way I can add some caveats and observations to the text based on this discussion, I didn't had too much time to think them through as I was going to the doctor for my annual check-up. Most of those will likely be common sense, but it is always good to put it down to words and we may find reason to discuss anyways.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26904_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26904\" data-vbnamecard=\"26904\">breggie</a> good write-up, I'll take some notes of it if I may. But I don't think the insta-death impact should be an issue. Not only does it make all the options more dangerous than needed, you're actually not in a form to which impact applies in the same way. There are no organs or even mass to be affected or deformed.<br /> <br /> ===============<br /> <br /> <i>General Movement:</i><br /> <br /> Unless otherwise specified for the specific kind of element, the natural state of any force is moving in a straight line. The basic success of the effect lets you direct this movement in some ways, but it is impossible to stop or act too much against it. As a rule of thumb, at 1 success you can't do anything that would be too obviously impossible for an educated observer.<br /> <br /> Extra successes can be used to generate more overtly alien movement. The first option is usually to retain human movement, in which case you can move around at your normal speed. This is extremely important to allow fine action and freedom of movement, although it won't yet let you ignore the medium a you move about. Added success beyond that work exactly as a normal Control Forces effect and must be decided in general terms at the casting. For example you can use 1 success to make fire exist for a short time in concrete, and as such you'll be able to walk between flammable surfaces as long as you don't spend much time on non-flammable ones.<br /> <br /> Additionally, you can still try to cast Magic while in this form. If you do, you can affect yourself with any Forces effect as if you were a common Pattern of the chosen type.<br /> <br /> <i>Gravity:</i><br /> <br /> Just as matter does, also energy falls, especially at a scientific paradigm, as a rule of thumb nothing flies freely. This is specially relevant when you're at a normal human speed and ignoring medium.<br /> <br /> There are caveats. Forces that move through propagation like Sound, Heat and Electricity ignore the rule for all practical purposes when moving in their own way. Gravity itself isn't ever affected, and moves freely in any direction.<br /> <br /> It's important to note, though, that most forces can travel at extreme speeds and as such jump really high or even at escape velocity. This isn't flight <i>per se</i> and don't offer a control surface once you leap, but ca still be used for extreme effect.<br /> <br /> Earth's Escape Velocity is about 11.186 Km/s (40,270 km/h; 25,020 mph; 36,700 ft/s). An upward jump at this speed or above will never come back to surface without further interference.<br /> <br /> While extra success may be used to allow flight for any force, the exact number of successes depends on the kind of force. YMMV, but between 1 to 3 seems like enough. Your elemental form may also impact if this flight will be vulgar, for whatever this is worth, or if it can be used as Instrument itself for the effect, depending on your paradigm.<br /> <br /> <i>Boundaries and Contact:</i><br /> <br /> Ease of movement as a force is a delicate balance. You're not yet able to switch your physicality on and off as you please. Instead, each force will change completely what is &quot;solid&quot;, &quot;fluid&quot; or &quot;immaterial&quot; for you, for the duration of the effect. If you can pass through something, then you can't touch or stand on this something. If you can stand on it, you can't pass through it. And since you're not actually solid, your Strength is 0 outside imparting changes that your kind of force should actually be able to.<br /> <br /> One important decision for the ST, that may or may not be at the character's choice upon casting or derive from paradigm, is what happens upon contact with surfaces that generate loss of energy, like light hitting a thin sheet of paper, since those surfaces can actually harm the character now. As a rule of thumb such surfaces should act as solids unless there is a conscious decision to traverse them. If not, then they universally act as lethal traps, but do not otherwise hinder movement.<br /> <br /> Remember also that you can't jump without solid ground under your feet.<br /> <br /> Finally, many forces rebound in some way when hitting anything they can't pass through. If the character impacts with a &quot;hard&quot; surface, they reflect more or less directly, depending on the specific force. It isn't a bad idea to set a success aside at casting to make your new body come at full stop in such a situation. Otherwise things can get excessively confusing too fast.<br /> <br /> <i>Awareness and Perception:</i><br /> <br /> Upon changing you keep your human conscience. Perception, though, may go through a lot of changes. Paradigm is important, but as a rule of thumb if it's decided that an elemental body does not perceive the world as a human being, then it perceives in regards to how the force moves.<br /> <br /> This perception is based on how hard it is to move through a surface, what effect you cause to that surface and what that surface causes to you. When something can't be interacted with, it may very well be &quot;invisible&quot; to a force body.<br /> <br /> An existence as a body of pure force is taxing to a mind without protection. Perceiving the world in such a way is deeply disorienting, taking time to adapt, while being pure energy may affect the mind if kept for too long. But the worse effect is that a human mind simply isn't made to deal with the sheer speed of most forces, so any action can end up being trickier than it seems.<br /> <br /> YMMV, but as a rule of thumb those effects shouldn't be a problem for a planned action. Knowing your environment beforehand helps to acclimate to weird perceptions, tracing routes for travel that makes full use of known boundaries is easier done than said, not the reverse. Even a half-ass plan before casting should be enough to work under most circumstances and enact simple but hyper-effective tasks.<br /> <br /> Other Spheres may help greatly in this process. Mind may hasten adaption, protect against eventual trauma and put your reaction on par with your speed. Correspondence may impart you greater awareness about your surroundings, routes and goal. Time and Entropy may give you enough precognition to act as if you actually knew what you're doing.<br /> <br /> <i>Physical Integrity:</i><br /> <br /> Any elemental body isn't a biological body for the effect's duration and don't receive damage in the same way as an living being. Most things won't even interact with a Forces body in a normal way, but even high speed impacts don't actually mean shit for a body without matter.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean it can't be hurt. Most force bodies are actually made of energy, and the amount of energy making up the &quot;body&quot; changes. This is what ultimately causes harm, as interacting with the environment robs you of some energy, as if you were leaving pieces of you behind.<br /> <br /> The exact amount of damage upon interacting with things varies, and since this isn't just a random amount of energy, but a self-contained mass woven together by magic, it shouldn't be much. As a rule of thumb damage should be the result of significant interactions, phasing through inhospitable material and so on. The particular cases should be electricity and sound: sound looses integrity fast on an open space, and maybe a better approach for it is to give it a hard distance limit instead of damage. Electricity can pass through anything but vacuum, but always at a loss that corresponds to the heat its passage generates, so it should receive and cause damage when passing through &quot;isolating&quot; materials (cause more than receive).<br /> <br /> Healing in this form is tricky. Just throwing energy at you won't integrate that energy to your pattern. You can't heal naturally and any healing magic need the same amount of Forces in addition to Life, along with a stable source of energy.<br /> <br /> Gravity, again, never suffer from those things. But it also don't interact with anything in any way resembling normality.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Light</b></i> - You decide your precise frequency in the electromagnetic spectrum or just exist as white light. Treat things as opaque, translucent, transparent or reflexive accordingly. You can touch opaque things and apply strength to heat them, instead of moving them. You can phase through translucent things, but takes damage dong so. You phase through transparent things always. Reflexive things are like soap for you in the best case, really hard to grasp, but ultimately solid. You can travel in any direction at the speed of light, but you do so at a straight line (affected by gravity as light is) until you stop or something redirects you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T05:49:52-08:00","id":1468260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468212#post1468212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... All the stuff ...</div> </div> </div> </div>WOW monteparnas, that is quite a write up. Very detailed and useful for any ST who may have to deal with this. Thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468212#post1468212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26904_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26904\" data-vbnamecard=\"26904\">breggie</a> good write-up, I'll take some notes of it if I may. But I don't think the insta-death impact should be an issue. Not only does it make all the options more dangerous than needed, you're actually not in a form to which impact applies in the same way. There are no organs or even mass to be affected or deformed.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <i><b>Light</b></i> - You decide your precise frequency in the electromagnetic spectrum or just exist as white light. Treat things as opaque, translucent, transparent or reflexive accordingly. You can touch opaque things and apply strength to heat them, instead of moving them. You can phase through translucent things, but takes damage dong so. You phase through transparent things always. Reflexive things are like soap for you in the best case, really hard to grasp, but ultimately solid. You can travel in any direction at the speed of light, but you do so at a straight line (affected by gravity as light is) until you stop or something redirects you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points all around. Hitting something as Light would not necessarily damage you, and as pointed out by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> you actually just bounce off of most surfaces. But not all surfaces are equal as you point out. <br /> <br /> Bouncing off of a flat mirror would be alright, as it would just redirect you. But bouncing off of an irregular reflective surface would scatter you in multiple directions, and at the speed you are going, within a single second you will be potentially scattered over a 600,000 km area (if you split in two opposite directions, each part is moving away from the source of the split at 300,000 km/s, so double that). That might ruin your day, even if it wouldn't be considered damage. An evil ST might make it take some time before you can reform your Light body, and you had better do so before the transformation effect wears off... *evil grin*.<br /> <br /> Bouncing off of an opaque surface will also scatter Light, but would also absorb at least some of it depending on it's &quot;color&quot; (not the scientific term). Some materials absorb almost all light that falls on them (like &quot;Vantablack&quot; <u><a href=\"https://thewonderofscience.com/phenomenon/2018/5/3/vantablack-the-darkest-material-on-earth\" target=\"_blank\">https://thewonderofscience.com/pheno...erial-on-earth</a></u> ) and others absorb much less.<br /> <br /> For these reasons I really like your idea of utilizing one success to pre-determine what happens to you when you collide with a surface. In most cases when hitting just about anything at the speed of light, you would probably want to immediately stop motion.<br /> <br /> But this begs the question... is turning into certain Forces a viable way to travel almost instantly without Correspondence/Data 3? With the dangers and considerations involved and since it likely needs Life 4/Forces 3/Mind ? and maybe even Time/Entropy for the best control. Someone with all that who is willing to have their character undergo such an invasive and traumatic transformation just to get to the other side of the planet at the speed of light because they don't have Correspondence? I'd say go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T08:20:29-08:00","id":1468274,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> great points you made. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26904_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26904\" data-vbnamecard=\"26904\">breggie</a><br /> <br /> For the intent I had in mind, which are primarily for defense and also quick escape/travel, I believe Gravity and Electromagnetism (more specifically gamma rays) are the best ones. <br /> <br /> -Gravity goes through anything and travels at lightspeed. The only thing is that you affect the world, by pulling very, very, VERY light objects (The gravity force of the entire planet results in 9,8 m/s2, so i believe your pull will be negligible). It's also invisible.<br /> <br /> - Gamma rays can only be absorbed by thick high atomic number materials, like lead or depleted uranium. Also travel at lightspeed and you are invisible.<br /> <br /> Either would work in a situation where you want to avoid any harm to your body and you can also travel very fast. You don't have to worry much about being reflected/absorbed since they are practically immune to that. <br /> <br /> Now, to answer your question, you need more spheres, and definitely more successes to travel using this spell than with Correspondence. Correspondence is truly instant, safe and precise. The biggest issue I see with the energy body travel is getting the path right in this form. You would probably have to adjust your position, unless you use Correspondence 1 to know exactly where is the place you wanna go and go there in a straight line. If you're not using Correspondence 1, then you will have to do a few lightspeed propagations until getting to the right location.<br /> <br /> Is it worth it? Well, if you don't have Correspondence, for sure! Is it better? No.<br /> <br /> It's definitely a good &quot;lemme get the fuck outta here&quot; when guns starts to shoot and things starts to explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-18-2021, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T11:20:53-08:00","id":1468285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468260#post1468260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bouncing off of an opaque surface will also scatter Light, but would also absorb at least some of it depending on it's &quot;color&quot; (not the scientific term). Some materials absorb almost all light that falls on them (like &quot;Vantablack&quot; <u><a href=\"https://thewonderofscience.com/phenomenon/2018/5/3/vantablack-the-darkest-material-on-earth\" target=\"_blank\">https://thewonderofscience.com/pheno...erial-on-earth</a></u> ) and others absorb much less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Color is a perfectly valid term to refer to specific electromagnetic frequency in most situations, even among physicists. It isn't exactly the same thing but the difference only matters in a few situations.<br /> <br /> In reality opacity always means light absorption if you're treating it as separate from reflexivity (which you should). But applying it in full would make all those effects far more dangerous than they really need to be.<br /> <br /> That's why I suggest treating it like just solid. First it is simpler to comprehend and run in a game. Second, it would be the kind of excessive realism that hinders the game instead of adding to it, as it just make the effect punishing for being against physics.<br /> <br /> But even if take at face value, this is most likely one of the first conundrums a student of Forces faces before reaching rank 3, and a developer of such effect find in the first experiments of the process. So the solution is likely to be baked into the effect from the start and be standard castng.<br /> <br /> Such solution being just the basic protection of the Pattern. Since you're not an amount of energy, but a self-contained Pattern, your touch don't impart any energy upon contact. Instead, the thing is solid for you and you can try to apply Strength if you want to have the effect of normal interaction. So a piece of paper painted with Vantablack is just solid for light, and a silencer or sound-proofed wall are just solid for sound.<br /> <br /> You know, instead of being death sentences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468274#post1468274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Gravity goes through anything and travels at lightspeed. The only thing is that you affect the world, by pulling very, very, VERY light objects (The gravity force of the entire planet results in 9,8 m/s2, so i believe your pull will be negligible). It's also invisible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are actually a few problems with gravity, but for as a getaway option they're probably negligible.<br /> <br /> First, gravity has a pull based on speed, not strength. You won't get near to winning over the entire planet's pull, so affected objects will move slowly and counter-forces have a good chance to win over you, but in terms of sheer strength your pull increases with the mass of the affected object, so you're actually pulling heavy things more strongly.<br /> <br /> Second, when nothing is solid to you you need even more attention to details, as you can get lost or end up inside something that will be problematic when the spell is over.<br /> <br /> You should be fine, though, as long as you don't stop at a single place for too long in this state and don't mess with too sensible materials. Your ST may decide to increase your effect to have something new happening, so stay alert.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468274#post1468274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Gamma rays can only be absorbed by thick high atomic number materials, like lead or depleted uranium. Also travel at lightspeed and you are invisible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only problem is that it is an extremely high-profile energy and even light contact may cause problems, and an entire human body is likely to be a huge amount of Gamma radiation. So beware your path to avoid side effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468274#post1468274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely a good &quot;lemme get the fuck outta here&quot; when guns starts to shoot and things starts to explode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes your travel destiny is just as specific as &quot;not here&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T17:52:14-08:00","id":1468315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468285#post1468285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> There are actually a few problems with gravity, but for as a getaway option they're probably negligible.<br /> <br /> First, gravity has a pull based on speed, not strength. You won't get near to winning over the entire planet's pull, so affected objects will move slowly and counter-forces have a good chance to win over you, but in terms of sheer strength your pull increases with the mass of the affected object, so you're actually pulling heavy things more strongly.<br /> <br /> Second, when nothing is solid to you you need even more attention to details, as you can get lost or end up inside something that will be problematic when the spell is over.<br /> <br /> You should be fine, though, as long as you don't stop at a single place for too long in this state and don't mess with too sensible materials. Your ST may decide to increase your effect to have something new happening, so stay alert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, I believe the pull would be negligible. You wouldn't be able to move an ant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468285#post1468285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only problem is that it is an extremely high-profile energy and even light contact may cause problems, and an entire human body is likely to be a huge amount of Gamma radiation. So beware your path to avoid side effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like giving cancer to people you phase through? Other than screwing people you get in contact which side effect are you talking about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468285#post1468285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes your travel destiny is just as specific as &amp;quot;not here&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T18:56:56-08:00","id":1468319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468315#post1468315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like giving cancer to people you phase through? Other than screwing people you get in contact which side effect are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly this, but you can also screw with electronic depending on where you cross through them, especially memories and processors.<br /> <br /> But the greater risk isn't the side effects you cause, but detection itself. Gamma radiation does leave a faint trail of ionized matter, and is itself detectable by a variety of equipment. While finding you isn't very likely at first, once you're detected this isn't a small deal, you're at the very least a cloud of high energy ionizing radiation. That's something no scientist will forget easily and no Technocrat will let pass.<br /> <br /> This also applies to gravity, although for now it would be even harder to be detected.<br /> <br /> I personally think that for your goals you should consider mastering all your options and varying their uses. That way you avoid becoming predictable, which will be far more dangerous to you when you assume a form that has many advantages, but also many specific ways to be explored by others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T19:46:07-08:00","id":1468324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468319#post1468319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly this, but you can also screw with electronic depending on where you cross through them, especially memories and processors.<br /> <br /> But the greater risk isn't the side effects you cause, but detection itself. Gamma radiation does leave a faint trail of ionized matter, and is itself detectable by a variety of equipment. While finding you isn't very likely at first, once you're detected this isn't a small deal, you're at the very least a cloud of high energy ionizing radiation. That's something no scientist will forget easily and no Technocrat will let pass.<br /> <br /> This also applies to gravity, although for now it would be even harder to be detected.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is to get intsngible to go through things and fast travel. In this scenario the mage won't be worried about messing any device. If you just want to pass unnoticed, you will be better becoming invisible with Forces 2. And if you just want to mass through a wall or door you can turn into gamma rays, pass carefully to avoid people and devices and turn back. I can't see this being a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468319#post1468319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that for your goals you should consider mastering all your options and varying their uses. That way you avoid becoming predictable, which will be far more dangerous to you when you assume a form that has many advantages, but also many specific ways to be explored by others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Although going gravity or gsmma rays both cover the objective pretty nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T23:35:16-08:00","id":1468331,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider carefully is how the ST makes the conversion from body to energy.<br /> <br /> Its easy to think it will be a relatively small amount, but that isn't necessarily the case. We are talking complete conversion into energy/force without loss. You should <i>be</i> more energy than the entire energy yield of your body after any form of consumption of it.<br /> <br /> From a scientific standpoint you should become so much energy that, true to the text of Life 4, your force-body keeps the exact same mass, weighting the same as before. For a 70 Kg adult that would be about 6.3 \u00d7 10<sup>1</sup><sup>8</sup> Joules, this is almost 30 times the energy yield of the Tsar Bomba, 7.8 times the eruption of Krakatoa in 1883 and enough to keep South Korea running in electricity for a year.<br /> <br /> You won't &quot;release&quot; all that at once, of course, not without dying, but that should give an estimation of just how much of a punch this form can pack or, more importantly, how much it can measure in instruments you eventually come in contact.<br /> <br /> That's why I say the ST may have &quot;ideas&quot; with this thing. Some forms are easier to figure in this way than others, as not all of them can be directly checked into the conversion formula (you need to be able to measure as a mass/energy relativistic system). Gravity is the trickier in our examples, but you should by all means <b>be</b> more gravity than you naturally <b>generate</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T06:22:32-08:00","id":1468343,"title":"","content":"Mixing modern physics and mage is always a strange proposition. For those unexpected things that &quot;should&quot; happen instead of the intended effect, I prefer to leave that for Paradox backlashes.<br /> <br /> Also, I wish I hadn't missed the photon mass debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T07:59:44-08:00","id":1468344,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>. Every aspect of this game can be ruined if we apply real science to it. So i think it is better to just ignore modern physics. Besides, the majority of those 10^18 Joules is consumed..uhm...transformed...into magick....because magick...<br /> <br /> This ammount of energy is too much even for paradox backlash.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I was just thinking. Just like this ammount of energy is present in our human bodies, but it is not released or used by this ammount in any form, the same could happen with element body. You indeed have this energy insise, but just like with your human body, you don't release it. We don't see humans turning into nukes. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm not quute sure I complety grasp this E=mc2 definition of mass=energy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-19-2021, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T10:41:58-08:00","id":1468356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468344#post1468344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>. Every aspect of this game can be ruined if we apply real science to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Observe that no write-up I made for the effect includes anything about the actual amount of energy, as I think that simply letting Strength use and Arete successes govern it should be enough. Although I don't completely agree with your statement, that was mainly a warning.<br /> <br /> First, that assuming it'll be a small amount of energy don't necessarily makes as much sense as it seems initially. You're turning your entire body into pure energy, this shouldn't be a small amount. Usually your body contains energy, instead of being completely turned into it.<br /> <br /> Second and more important, that if you're not the ST you must be prepared for the entire gamut the actual ST's interpretation could go.<br /> <br /> <b><i>My</i></b> interpretation is that it wouldn't be negligible just because I find it boring and pointless. Also because you may want one day to actually use the force in your favor, so the option must be built in.<br /> <br /> But YMMV, and I won't say to another ST that they're wrong in reading it like this, as long as objective rules are respected. And this case does have some latitude in regards to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468344#post1468344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, the majority of those 10^18 Joules is consumed..uhm...transformed...into magick....because magick...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the majority of this energy is simply still you. Your body made of energy is, still, a body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468344#post1468344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This ammount of energy is too much even for paradox backlash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not look just at this effect to understand the amount of energy. Letting physics aside and talking only Mage, we are talking about the maximum energy output that can be derived from your body with a perfect spell, short of generating more energy.<br /> <br /> Think about the perfect conversion, a Master using two or three rituals with Entropy, Forces, Life Matter and Prime to unravel your Pattern completely, taking every bit of Quintessence possible from it, storing all the energy you had on you in other forms (your heat, fat, electricity to run heart, muscles and brain, and more), then using every single scrap into a dedicated effect just to produce energy.<br /> <br /> While you can't use all this energy (it's still locked into your Pattern, or you would cease to be), this is the amount of energy that makes your forces body. Indeed it may be even greater, as even a master may loose some potential in the process. Just from the fact that a vampire can suck up to 10 Quint from a healthy human and still leave a Matter Pattern behind, we can assume a baseline of at the very least 11 to 13 Quint making up just the physical Pattern of a person.<br /> <br /> And why this is for sure the amount of energy composing this body? There's a sense of Conservation of Quintessence is built in Mage. This amount only presume as limitation that you don't use any effect that creates something out of nothing, only converts. Your effect of element body isn't destroying your Pattern, just changing it, so the result must contain the same amount of stuff for other Spells to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468344#post1468344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the same could happen with element body. You indeed have this energy insise, but just like with your human body</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the case, indeed, hence my biggest worry is detection, not side effects. You're a non-dispersive body of force, most of it is effectively locked into being your body. Lets assume, indeed, 30 times the explosive potential of the Tsar Bomba, but you're not exploding.<br /> <br /> But if you're, say, all of that as concentrated Gamma Rays in the shape and size of a person, passing next a Geiger counter, the poor thing will go crazy with the sheer amount of radiation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467680-turn-body-into-elemental-forces?p=1468344#post1468344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm not quute sure I complety grasp this E=mc2 definition of mass=energy...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's tricky, but basically it is to be taken at face value. It's almost like if matter and energy were states of the same thing, just solid may turn into liquid, under the right conditions matter turns into energy and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> Lets see some examples. The eruption of Krakatoa in 1883 released about 8\u00d710<sup>17</sup> Joules of energy. Imagine an electrical generator could be put there and turn most of this energy into electricity, lets say exactly 5\u00d710<sup>17</sup> J, and store that into a nearby system of batteries.<br /> <br /> The battery system is closed but for the electrical feed. It doesn't matter how they change to store this energy, no matter leaves or enters the system in any way. If you weight those batteries during the process, they literally would become a little more than 5.5 Kg heavier just with the added energy.<br /> <br /> No actual substance, no becoming a heavier element, <b>not even the weight of additional electrons</b>. If there are additional electrons or anything of the like, its mass would enter the system above those 5.5 Kg. This is simply the weight of the energy itself. It's mass as normal, is affected by gravity, has its own inertia, everything. That's how a photon, having 0 intrinsic mass, still has momentum, because it actually does have mass equal 0 + its energy state. That's also why it is impossible to reach the speed of light, because as your speed increases, the added kinetic energy has its own inertia and must also be moved by extra kinetic energy.<br /> <br /> Some situations convert matter and energy into each other. If that electricity is directly converted into matter, it will become 5.5 Kg of whatever. And the secret of an atomic bomb is precisely that it doesn't simply release stored energy, but part of its matter truly ceases to be as such and becomes energy, not vapor or plasma, but energy itself.<br /> <br /> Curiously that also means that under a strict scientific paradigm your force-body, if made of energy, still weights the same after full conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T22:28:05-08:00","id":1468383,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Yes, like I pointed out later in my edit, the energy in the element body is locked just as the energy is locked in regular human body.<br /> <br /> About detection, gamma rays are very, very, VERY tiny, 10^-12 meters wavelength. The scale of atoms nuclei. It is literally microscopic and can pass through atoms empty space. Geigers can detect it, but it is so tiny that it is not efficient in doing so. Geigers are better at detecting alpha and beta radiation, that are much bigger. I know the amount the mage will turn into is big and might be detected, but it wouldn't explode the detector. Also, one would probably think the detector is broken before thinking there is such an ammount of gamma rays floating around. Unless it's a Technocrat. But then, you're kinda screwed anyway. You will easier be detected in your regular body then in your gamma ray body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-20-2021, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}